{
  "abstract": "This Lean and Mathlib development proves Graffiti.pc Conjecture 261. For a finite simple connected graph G of order at least two, let S be its degree-two vertices and let L(G) be the maximum number of leaves over its spanning trees. The total domination number of G is at least 2|N_G(S) \\ S| / L(G), where N_G(S) consists of the vertices adjacent to some vertex of S. The formal proof combines a count of edges incident to S with a leaf bound from a spanning tree preserving a total dominating set. The compared theorem states the inequality with rational division.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Liam Kinnally"
    }
  ],
